        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Burn pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 3/10; described as more annoying than anything."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported skin changes after burn"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Immediate redness and tightness over cheeks, nose, forehead and anterior neck. On day 1, small blisters developed on both upper cheeks and popped on their own; now dry and tight with mild pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Burn examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Forehead, nasal bridge, both malar areas, anterior neck to upper chest involved, with a clear T-shirt line and safety-glasses border pattern. Forehead, nose and neck erythematous, warm and mildly tender with intact sensation. Both upper cheeks have 2–3 cm healing superficial partial-thickness areas where blisters ruptured; now pink and moist, with no slough or pus. Skin soft with no tight eschar or circumferential neck burn. No charring; minimal singeing of eyebrows and sideburns. No clinical cellulitis at present. Estimated TBSA approximately 5–6%."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Eye symptoms and examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Brief bright flash with spots seen for a few minutes, then settled. Mild grittiness in both eyes the first night, now resolved. Currently denies eye pain, photophobia, blurred vision, foreign-body sensation and reduced vision. No periorbital oedema; lids open fully and no burns at lid margins. Mild conjunctival injection without chemosis. PERRLA, EOMI, visual acuity grossly normal and able to read a poster. No photophobia. Fluorescein and Wood lamp examination was offered and declined after risks were explained."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Airway and respiratory symptoms and examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies hoarseness, dysphagia, shortness of breath at the time of injury or since, cough and soot in the mouth. Oropharynx clear, no soot or marked posterior pharyngeal erythema. Voice normal, no stridor; neck supple and trachea midline. Chest clear bilaterally."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Systemic symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies fever, chills, nausea and vomiting; reports feeling otherwise well."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance and examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert, well appearing, speaking in full sentences and in no acute distress. Heart sounds dual with no added sounds. Neurologically grossly non-focal; gait normal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Functional effects of burn"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Tightness makes opening the mouth wide and shaving uncomfortable."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Intermittent low back soreness"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient briefly mentioned occasional low back soreness from work; further assessment deferred, with advice to book a separate appointment if ongoing or worsening."
      }
    },
